# No wildcard targets that hide commands

Do not use `%` pattern rules to forward or broadcast targets. Spell every target out so the file is self-documenting.

`%` is only allowed when the stem is a program argument (`$*`), not a hidden target name.

```make
# BAD
services.vpr.%:
	$(MAKE) -C services/vpr $*

# GOOD
services.vpr.start:
	$(MAKE) -C services/vpr start

# GOOD - % is an argument
kill-port.%:
	./scripts/kill-port $*
```
